course: dictionary
lesson: 4124
title: Two meanings in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «A glassy lake reflected the snowy mountains.» A lake cannot be made of glass, but the clues say it is still and clear, so glassy means smooth, shiny and clear, like glass.
explain: «Her glassy eyes stared at the wall after the bad news.» Eyes do not turn into glass. The clues are the bad news and the staring at the wall, so glassy here means blank and without expression.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. A smooth, shiny lake makes sense. Blank eyes that stare after bad news make sense. If your meaning does not fit, try the other meaning.
fact: «Glassy» means smooth, shiny and clear, like glass.
fact: «Glassy eyes» look blank and without expression, often because of tiredness, illness or being upset.
fact: Obsidian is a glassy rock, formed when volcanic lava cools quickly.
fact: «A boiled sweet is sugar syrup boiled until it sets hard, glassy and see-through, really a kind of sugar glass.»
fact: Some words have more than one meaning, so always check the context before you decide.
exercise: «A glassy lake reflected the snowy mountains.» What does glassy mean here? | Rough and full of rocks | Noisy and wild | Warm and sandy | *Smooth, shiny and clear, like glass
exercise: «Her glassy eyes stared at the wall after the bad news.» What does glassy suggest? | *Blank and without expression, as if she is upset | Happy and full of fun | Dirty and muddy | Wide open with excitement
exercise: Find and copy the word in «The boiled sweet was hard, glassy and see-through» that means clear, like glass. | sweet | hard | *glassy | boiled
test: «After the long shift, his glassy eyes could barely stay open.» What does glassy mean here? | Clear and sparkling with joy | Full of tears | Smooth and shiny | *Blank and tired, without expression
test: «The pond was glassy at dawn, with not a ripple on it.» What does glassy mean here? | Deep and dark | Rough and choppy | *Smooth and shiny, like glass | Muddy and brown
exam: Which meaning fits «a glassy stare» best? | Wet and cold | Happy and bright | Shiny and clear, like a window | *Blank and without expression
